  "hypothesis": "An absolute Laplace-metric eigenvalue floor in prior units (0.5) instead of the relative 1e-4 floor stops clipping real posterior directions on edge-on fits (13/32 clipped in the audit): fewer steps on those fits, no change where the relative floor never engaged, posteriors unchanged.",
  "reason": "One-knob arm of the fit-initialization toolkit (fit.eig_floor_mode prior, eig_floor 0.5) against the w200 reference.",
  "conclusion": "SUPPORTED. 14/32 fits (truth cosi >= 0.32, no clipping either way) reproduce the reference bit-for-bit (identical steps and posteriors). On the 18 edge-on fits the floor engaged 0-5 times (condition number up to 2.4e5 instead of pegged at 1e4) and steps changed 0.42-1.45x with median 1.00; both reference escalations (g5_r90 rhat 1.11, g15_r90 1.06) pass first-pass at 0.42-0.44x the steps. First-pass fails 0/32 (ref 2), sum steps 2.16M vs 2.40M (-10%), sum wall 23.3k vs 25.7k s (-9%), max fit wall 1791 vs 2955 s, clean steps/draw 48 vs 42 (the added draws are on fits that previously escalated). Posteriors agree (max 0.2 sigma, widths 1.00). Caveat: g5_r90 is again in the counter-rotating wrong mode (legacy unbounded MAP; v0 -104 vs truth +15) and passes the gate at rhat 1.011 -- the floor does not address that; the bounded MAP (988356) does.",
